<title>POLAND: Polish crop ratings fall in rainy July 1-10.</title>
<headline>Polish crop ratings fall in rainy July 1-10.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's Meteorology and Water Management Institute (IMGW) said crop evaluations in the first 10 days of July were worse than in the previous 10 days and corresponding 1996 levels but held above five-year averages.</p>
<p>&quot;Heavy rainfall occuring mainly in Southern regions of the country created huge losses in agriculture,&quot; it said in a statement, adding that IMGW's field work had been halted or delayed in many areas because of the resulting flood.</p>
<p>Ratings are made three times a month based on the condition and development of crops on a scale of one to five, with five the highest grade.</p>
<p> POLISH CROP RATINGS   JULY 10   JUNE 30  1996  5-YR AVG</p>
<p> Wheat (winter)	    3.4	 3.6     3.6	3.4</p>
<p> Wheat (summer)	    3.5	 3.7     3.6	3.4</p>
<p> Rye			   3.4	 3.7     3.6	3.4</p>
<p> Barley (spring)	   3.5	 3.8     3.5	3.3</p>
<p> Rapeseed (winter)	 3.0	 3.1     2.9	n.a.</p>
<p> Oats			  3.4	 3.7     3.6	3.3</p>
<p> Sugar beets		 3.7	 3.7     3.7	3.4</p>
<p> Potatoes		    3.5	 3.7     3.6	3.4</p>
<p>--Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
